Description: keyword-triggered local RAG hook for Claude Code
 claude-rag-hook is a UserPromptSubmit hook for Claude Code, the
 Anthropic terminal AI coding tool. Type "rag: <question>" in Claude
 Code; the hook walks back through your cwd, looks for an index, embeds
 the query against the chosen embedder, retrieves the top-K relevant
 chunks from a per-folder LanceDB index, and prepends them to the
 prompt as a context block. Claude Code receives an enriched prompt and
 answers normally.
 .
 Unlike MCP-driven local RAG (where the model decides when to retrieve)
 the hook is keyword-triggered and deterministic: the user types the
 trigger, the hook retrieves; otherwise it is a no-op. Zero token
 overhead on prompts that do not start with the trigger.
 .
 Ships with a fastembed embedder (lazy import; install via pip extras),
 an OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings client, and an optional hydra-llm
 interop layer that reuses an installed embedder catalog and per-folder
 .hydra-index/ stores. A small per-user warm daemon keeps the embedder
 loaded for sub-second retrieval.
 .
 DISCLAIMER: This software reads files inside any folder you index and
 stores chunked text plus embeddings of those files at
 <folder>/.claude-rag-index/. Retrieved chunks are sent to Anthropic
 when the trigger fires. It is provided AS IS, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
 KIND. The author is not liable for any damage to data, hardware, or
 system, or for the content of model output. Audit what you index. See
 /usr/share/doc/claude-rag-hook/README.md for the full text.
